[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2652012903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102634#issuecomment-2652012903","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102634","id":2652012903,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eEoFn","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T20:36:43Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T20:36:43Z","body":"MacOS doesn't fully support OpenGL. One of the things missing is timestamp functionality which is needed for measuring GPU time (I think it is implemented on intel Macs though).\n\nUnfortunately that means that the visual profiler can't be implemented on MacOS when using the Compatibility renderer. To be clear, it is implemented, Apple just chooses to ignore the timestamps. \n\nAlso, to make matters worse, the OpenGL Profiler has been deprecated for years and doesn't work on Apple Silicon. So on Apple Silicon devices your only option is to use Metal for profiling (which implies switching to the mobile or forward+ renderer)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions"